  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Writing Expression from Patterns</title>
<para>Find the number of dots in Step 5, and write an expression to find \(n\) number of dots.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5f6a3a4e86b3cacc1de7c66c1684973c2869bf42"/></media></figure></para>
<para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Make a table to help you find the pattern. </para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Step number
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
        Number of dots
      </entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        7
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        10
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        13
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Notice that the start has 2 rows and 2 columns, or 4 dots.
  Each step adds a row of 2 dots, plus 1 more dot.
  So, each step adds 3 dots.</para>
<para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Continuing this linear pattern, Step 5 would have 19 dots. </para>
<para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - An expression could be \(3n+4\). 
  This is a linear expression. </para>
<title>Try It: Writing Expression from Patterns</title>

<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find the number of dots in Step 5, and write an expression to find \(n\) number of dots.</para>
    <para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/48e390686ad23411dd3af33c33aa761446de1202"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Here is how to write an expression from a pattern:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
          Step
        </entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
          Number of dots
        </entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          2
        </entry>
        <entry>
          9
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
        <entry>
          19
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
  <para>Each step has that number of dots squared, then doubled, and then one is added.</para>
  <para>So, Step 5 would have 51 dots.</para>
  <para>The expression would be \(2n^2+1\), where \(n\) is the step number.</para>
  <para>This is a quadratic expression.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
